{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457469-beckett\u2019s-second-jyhad-diary","id":1457469,"title":"Beckett\u2019s second Jyhad Diary","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-23T05:12:55-07:00","id":1457469,"title":"Beckett\u2019s second Jyhad Diary","content":"Here\u2019s a thought exercise.<br /> <br /> Like many on here I consider Beckett\u2019s Jyhad Diary one of the very best books published for Vampire the Masquerade. Its role in establishing lore for V20, and as a transition to/starting block for the lore of V5, has been vital. Its value is incalculable. That being said, with the lore progression seen with the various V5 books it is already somewhat obsolete.<br /> <br /> So, with that in mind, if you were creating a sequel to that book to incorporate/explore the V5 lore (keeping in mind I mean the existing official lore, not speculation on as yet unreleased information for the Sabbat and Second inquisition) how might you plan out the chapters, with broad-stroke subject topics? What subjects/locations/characters/events do you want to see examined specifically?<br /> <br /> Create for me a contents page of what YOU would like to be explored in a hypothetical second Beckett\u2019s Jyhad Diary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25360-antihierophant24","name":"antihierophant24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T05:13:52-07:00","id":1457470,"title":"","content":"For example, I\u2019d personally like to see a chapter set in Edinburgh which explores Roger De Camden.<br /> Specifically the balance between the roles he has as Prince of an ostensibly Camarilla city whilst still being a major mover and shaker in the newly united Hecata Family. Throw into this the imminent end of the Promise of 1528 and his OTHER role as Pater of the Cult of Mithras, and I\u2019d like to see how all of these ideas balance out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25360-antihierophant24","name":"antihierophant24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T09:36:03-07:00","id":1457483,"title":"","content":"Something updating Vancouver &amp;/or Dark Colony that, afaik, are the only canon city/region books not adressed in some way by the storylines from BJD - since &quot;War Across Dixie&quot; while not adressing any one book in particular kind of covers Atlanta, New Orleans (&amp; ST's Handbook to the Sabbat's Birmingham, Alabama).<br /> <br /> (Ok, technically Cairo is another city book not adressed by BJD, but since it's a Revised era book, i'd guess there's much less necessity of updating on its case)<br /> <br /> As an aside, i always find mildly delusional/ironic how Beckett never, ever adresses the far from mild parallels between the effects of the False Caine's passage in Berlin and the &quot;real&quot; (?) one's more subdued participation in the events in LA on Bloodlines. A fascinating bit of self-denial, imho. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Seeing &quot;Jyhad Journals&quot; by other (in)famous noddists that are <b>not</b> Beckett - like Aristotle DeLaurent, Dr. Mortius, Ayisha Jocastian, Oculo (Beckett's longtime Nosferatu associate) and Bindusara, for a few examples - along with a few extra noddist/gehenist pamphlets in the vein of the Book of the Grave War such as, for instance, the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Codex_of_the_Damned\" target=\"_blank\">Codex of Damned</a>, the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Incunabulum_Kupalam\" target=\"_blank\">Incunabulum Kupalam</a>, Le Myst\u00e9rie Rubix (Rubrique? Rubix afaik is just gibberish - and an ancient <a href=\"https://hellraiser.fandom.com/wiki/Puzzle_Box\" target=\"_blank\">french occult tome being a rubik cube</a> makes no sense) or some brand new or <a href=\"https://vtmb.fandom.com/wiki/Vampyr_Apocrypha\" target=\"_blank\">fake</a> stuff would be quite nice too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-23-2021, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T10:56:24-07:00","id":1457492,"title":"","content":"The one thing conspicuously missing from Beckett's Jyhad Diary is The Ravnos and The Week of Nightmares, which is something we know happened in the v5 timeline. BJD in fact sets this up with the Eye of Hazimel. There's always been questions about Beckett's actual Clan, and one of my best guesses is Ravnos. Would explain his particular archaeological compulsion, and then not caring about following through once he finds something. Would explain why The Week of Nightmares is not in the Journal, it's what ends up being the end of Beckett and why his Diary gets published. So I'm not sure I believe there could be a second BJD by Beckett. However, what I might like to see would be a sort of tour book of various cities, which would be a way of showing differing governing structures and responses to the events of BJD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27018-wstarter","name":"wstarter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T11:22:10-07:00","id":1457495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wstarter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457469-beckett\u2019s-second-jyhad-diary?p=1457492#post1457492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one thing conspicuously missing from Beckett's Jyhad Diary is The Ravnos and The Week of Nightmares, which is something we know happened in the v5 timeline. BJD in fact sets this up with the Eye of Hazimel. There's always been questions about Beckett's actual Clan, and one of my best guesses is Ravnos. Would explain his particular archaeological compulsion, and then not caring about following through once he finds something. Would explain why The Week of Nightmares is not in the Journal, it's what ends up being the end of Beckett and why his Diary gets published. So I'm not sure I believe there could be a second BJD by Beckett. However, what I might like to see would be a sort of tour book of various cities, which would be a way of showing differing governing structures and responses to the events of BJD.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting alternate take on the character and some aspects of both book and the metaplot for sure. The simpler explanation might be that BJD was still very much a V20 product, dancing around the issue of Revised Era events, hinting at them but keeping them optional overall, unlike V5 that took other directions, but &quot;Beckett as secretly Ravnos&quot; (instead of Gangrel as has been repeatedly implied &amp;/or stated) and wholy dead, true or not, could make a good starting point for a story arc indeed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of &quot;responses to the events of BJD&quot;, in my own chronicle i decided to make the Bloodline's taxi driver and the &quot;False Caine&quot; of Berlin one and the same, while making up <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Legacy_of_Kain\" target=\"_blank\">the Legacy</a>, a society of wannabe noddists that follows his tracks and adhere to a nomadic lifestyle inspired by it in which they have adopted a large number of Caitiffs &amp; thin-bloods as converts and causing all kinds of trouble wherever they pass by sheer virtue of their numbers, proselytizing and overall nosiness.<br /> <br /> Along the way they also gathered the <a href=\"https://vtmb.fandom.com/wiki/Vampyr_Apocrypha\" target=\"_blank\">Apocrypha</a>, fragments of the <a href=\"https://vtmb.fandom.com/wiki/Ankaran_Sarcophagus\" target=\"_blank\">Sarcophagus</a> and the mummy of &quot;<a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Messerach\" target=\"_blank\">Messerach</a>&quot;, that they have been studying since.<br /> One of their theories is he's actually a still torpid Cappadocian that disguised his nature from other kindred through Mortis/Necromancy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-23-2022, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T11:56:41-07:00","id":1457500,"title":"","content":"The interesting thing about Beckett is that he wasn't used as the Gangrel signature character in the novels, where as the others like Anatole and Lucita were. There's also been a number of questions about what his Clan actually is. Mnemosyne is one that I've heard brought up. The Ravnos take makes a lot of sense to me, and the other possibility I might see is Baali as the Lore of the Bloodlines section on Baali almost wink at the idea of Beckett in some of there write-ups.<br /> <br /> My general point is that I feel like BJD went and covered so much of the metaplot that it would be hard to then follow that up with an equal amount and equal quality of metaplot. Showing how the world has shifted because of the metaplot is the most sensible follow-up I could see. That would work to show how all of this might matter to your typical chronicle. What is the new lay of the land for the four sects in their cities? Cover their restructuring and night-to-night with some hints of metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27018-wstarter","name":"wstarter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T13:33:35-07:00","id":1457506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wstarter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457469-beckett\u2019s-second-jyhad-diary?p=1457500#post1457500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The interesting thing about Beckett is that he wasn't used as the Gangrel signature character in the novels, where as the others like Anatole and Lucita were. There's also been a number of questions about what his Clan actually is. Mnemosyne is one that I've heard brought up. The Ravnos take makes a lot of sense to me, and the other possibility I might see is Baali as the Lore of the Bloodlines section on Baali almost wink at the idea of Beckett in some of there write-ups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, <b>some </b>novels had to use new blood to represent their clan, eh?<br /> <br /> Yeah, the Mnemosyne thing is a big deal - but then, so it would be for DeLaurent too. I can see possibilities on making him something else, but i prefer to stick with him as Gangrel - among other things because then i can use the gender-flipped Indiana Jones archetype image from Clanbook Gangrel for his childe Marie. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, speaking of the Week of Nightmares - check out pages 327-343 of BJD.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wstarter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457469-beckett\u2019s-second-jyhad-diary?p=1457500#post1457500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My general point is that I feel like BJD went and covered so much of the metaplot that it would be hard to then follow that up with an equal amount and equal quality of metaplot. Showing how the world has shifted because of the metaplot is the most sensible follow-up I could see. That would work to show how all of this might matter to your typical chronicle. What is the new lay of the land for the four sects in their cities? Cover their restructuring and night-to-night with some hints of metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm of two minds on that - it works for BJD where they are narratives to be read as much as springboards for STs to start up story arcs or whole chronicles of their own. But sometimes introducing too much in the way of &quot;NPC colaterals&quot; can become problematic and lead to broken base issues among others things, as shown by Revised era and V5's takes on each.<br /> <br /> Leaving things like they are in BJD is mighty convenient to mix metaplot with one's ideas for its own group and table - my &quot;Legacy&quot; chronicle is basically a blend of the &quot;Anarch Freefall&quot; and &quot;False Caine&quot; plotlines with a wannabe noddist cult/proto-sect of PC goofs and confused kindred of all ages mixed in trying to make sense of things (and creating even more trouble wherever they pass through their liberty with spreading lore, open camaradie/coordination &amp; sheer numbers.<br /> <br /> Damn, the &quot;cell leaders&quot; of the Legacy are simply whoever has Astral Projection to set up &quot;spiritual forums&quot; where they debate and exchange info from anywhere in the world between cabals. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-23-2021, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T13:48:56-07:00","id":1457508,"title":"","content":"I'd love a Maxwell as Prince of Gary situation. Maybe with Arthur and Allicia as part of their court.<br /> <br /> A Beckett discussing business with Kevin Jackson would be awesome, especially if Beckett points out how the Lasombra played him like a fiddle.<br /> <br /> Maybe also a Hesha discussing the split between Anarch and Independent Ministry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T14:29:27-07:00","id":1457512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457469-beckett\u2019s-second-jyhad-diary?p=1457508#post1457508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love a Maxwell as Prince of Gary situation. Maybe with Arthur and Allicia as part of their court.<br /> <br /> A Beckett discussing business with Kevin Jackson would be awesome, especially if Beckett points out how the Lasombra played him like a fiddle.</div> </div> </div> </div>You just can't stop seeing him poke holes at the sore spots of people in power he was better off not messing with, eh? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What makes me remember the PCs doing exactly with him when discussing &quot;the Cabbie&quot; and what were his arguments for the supposed falsehood of the &quot;Berlin Caine&quot;. Fun times were had.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457469-beckett\u2019s-second-jyhad-diary?p=1457508#post1457508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe also a Hesha discussing the split between Anarch and Independent Ministry.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be interesting indeed, though i imagine him being closer to the Fire Court/Ortodoxy, i could see being wrong on that and Hesha being anywhere in the spectrum depending on circunstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-21-2021, 08:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T16:29:58-07:00","id":1457525,"title":"","content":"In addition to sections dealing with Gary, Vancouver, and the aftermath of the Week of Nigthmares,I would like a visit the ruins of Ceoris, the Bohemian Grove (where my head cannon puts Carna), Beckett visiting with the leadership of an Ashirra City, and Gobekli Tepe,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457469-beckett\u2019s-second-jyhad-diary?p=1457508#post1457508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Beckett discussing business with Kevin Jackson would be awesome, especially if Beckett points out how the Lasombra played him like a fiddle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that Beckett has the social finesse of a flaming chainsaw, that would be an interesting encounter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T12:17:21-07:00","id":1457587,"title":"","content":"Yeah, a pretty decent summary of V5 events would be:<br /> <br /> * The Second Inquisition (duh)<br /> * The Council of Prague from Theo Bell's perspective<br /> * The Council of Prague from Lucinde's perspective<br /> * The Ministry/Church of Set split with Hesha and Beckett<br /> * The expelling of the Brujah<br /> * The creation of the New Anarchs (possibly talking to Rudi)<br /> * The Fall of Berlin to the Anarchs<br /> * Beckett visiting Tokyo and meeting its neonate Tzimisce Prince<br /> * Beckett and Kevin Jackson re: The Lasombra<br /> * Beckett and Let the Streets Run Red (Gary and Milwaukee chapter)<br /> * Beckett and a discussion of the new Blood Cults (Cults of the Blood Gods chapter)<br /> * The takeover of Mexico City by Fiorenza<br /> * The status of New York City under Shadows of New York/Coteries of New York<br /> * The CHAPTERS chapter<br /> * The Vermillion Wedding (which Beckett will undoubtedly mock Victoria Ash over)<br /> * The Week of Nightmares aftermath<br /> * Beckett talking with the Hecata abouf Hecata-esque things<br /> * A discussion of the Gehenna War<br /> * A discussion of the Sabbat<br /> * Marcus Vitel as &quot;Anarch&quot; Emperor of Washington D.C.<br /> * Maybe canonizing the first couple of seasons of LA by Night by having Beckett talk to Ramona or Baron Temple<br /> * The comic book's first arc<br /> <br /> I mean, there is a massive amount of metaplot developments spread across multiple books<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervil